<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12717" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēflŭus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		defluo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>flowing down;</i> or transf., <i>moving downwards, going</i> or <i>falling
			down</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gradus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 9, 325</span></i>
			: caesaries, <i>long and flowing</i>, Prud.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 13, 30: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">splendor ab alto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 1, 3, 53</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Esp.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vasculum (in which a liquid runs down),</span>”
				<i>a water-clock</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 3, p. 130, 21</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
